-- title:
--   Adic Galois representation from a Hecke eigenplane
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero level $N$, a set $S$ of naturals, and a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}'$ which is a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and with $p$ in its maximal ideal; let $K$ be a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}'$ and $M$ a finite free $\mathcal{O}'$-module. Suppose given a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(M)$, a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from the polynomial ring $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(M)$, and a ring homomorphism $\chi$ to $\mathcal{O}'$ from the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q \mid N$ prime, $q \notin S$). Assume: (i) there is a $K$-subspace $W \subseteq K \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} M$ of dimension $2$, stable under all base-changed $\rho_M(\sigma)$, on which the base change of $T_M(X_\ell)$ acts by the image of $\chi(T_\ell)$ for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, and on which the restriction of the base change of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ has trace $\chi(T_\ell)$ whenever $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and induces $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$; (ii) for such $\ell$, $A$ and $\sigma$ the relation $\rho_M(\sigma)^2 - T_M(X_\ell)\rho_M(\sigma) + \ell = 0$ holds on $M$; (iii) for every prime $q \nmid N$ with $q \neq p$ and every valuation subring $P$ with $q$ a nonunit of $P$, the image in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ acts trivially on $M$; (iv) $\rho_M$ is adically continuous, i.e. for each $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $\rho_M(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}^n M$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise. Then there exists an adic Galois representation over $\mathcal{O}'$, that is a finite free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with an adically continuous monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(V)$, such that $\rho(\sigma)$ has characteristic polynomial $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ over $\mathcal{O}'$ for every $\ell$, $A$, $\sigma$ as in (i), and such that for every prime $q \nmid N$ with $q \neq p$ the inertia subgroups at all valuation subrings over $q$ act trivially on $V$. The prime $p$ enters only through the conditions $p \in \mathfrak{m}$ and $q \neq p$.
--
--   This is the lattice-and-characteristic-polynomial step in the construction of the two-dimensional $p$-adic Galois representation attached to a weight-two Hecke eigensystem: a Galois-stable eigenplane in $K \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} M$, together with the operator form of the Eichler–Shimura relation, is converted into an integral rank-two representation with Frobenius characteristic polynomials $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$. It is used in the passage from a newform to its associated adic representation, in the form cited by the newform statement producing a representation with prescribed behaviour of inertia.
